1. Introduction

An Operating System (OS) manages hardware and software on a computer and allows users to perform various actions. It manages memory, files, applications, devices, and security [1], [5].

This project will look at the different ways an OS can assist a small business. Windows 11 will be used as the main Operating System and Ubuntu Linux as a comparison.

The project looks at user accounts, process management, batch processing, security, real Time Simulation, resource optimisation, hardware performance, and user interaction. This is important as it helps the business protect information, manage computers and increase productivity for employees.

