7. Question Five – Real Time Simulation

Real time systems are designed to respond to events within certain time frames. This can be demonstrated by using a local web server.

This is not a true hard real time operating system.

7.1 Start Server

Ubuntu has the Python HTTP server module. To start the server type:

python3 -m http.server 8000

This will list the files in the current working directory. Python describe this as a simple HTTP server [10].

Figure 5.1 – Ubuntu Python Web Server Running

7.2 Access & Monitor

To access the server open a browser and type:

http://localhost:8000

The browser will request the files and the server will show the available files or index page.

You can use the top command in another terminal to monitor processes and resources.

top

This will help the administrator see what process is running and what the CPU and RAM usage is.

The service may slow down if there are many users accessing it. The Python server is a good choice for demonstration but is not recommended for use in production as it only has basic security features [10].

