8. Question Six – Resource Optimisation

Resource optimisation will help improve how the CPU, RAM, and Storage are used on the computer. If there are high resources it can cause the computer to slow down and effect productivity.

8.1 Monitor & Improve

The Task Manager on Windows can show what the CPU, RAM, and Disk usage is [2]. The administrator can see which applications are using too much resources.

Improvements that could be made:

- Close any unnecessary applications.
- Turn off any unnecessary applications to start.
- Use Storage to delete temporary files.
- Don’t have too many demanding applications open.

Storage Sense can help delete temporary files [7].

