9. Question Seven – Hardware

The hardware will affect how quickly the Operating System can complete tasks. Important hardware would be the CPU, RAM, and Storage.

9.1 RAM

RAM is used to store information temporarily whilst applications are running. If a computer doesn’t have much RAM it may struggle if there are a lot of applications open.

The more RAM the computer will be able to run more applications. 8Gb would be a good starting point for basic office use. 16Gb+ would be better for more demanding multi-tasking.

9.2 HDD & SSD

An HDD uses moving parts to read/write information. An SSD uses flash memory and has no moving parts.

SSD’s generally have faster boot and application load times. This would be a good choice for ApliSoft.

9.3 Check Specifications

The Task Manager on Windows can show CPU and RAM information by going into the Performance tab.

Using PowerShell you can view the physical disks by typing:

Get-PhysicalDisk

This will help identify what storage devices you have and what media type they are.

